WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.479 --> 00:00:03.831
(upbeat music)

00:00:03.831 --> 00:00:05.136
- The main thing people
think about Compton

00:00:05.136 --> 00:00:09.049
is you go into Compton and
everybody's gang-banging at you

00:00:09.049 --> 00:00:13.173
and shooting at you but
it's really not like that.

00:00:13.173 --> 00:00:15.779
There have been times that
people have made rude comments

00:00:15.779 --> 00:00:17.737
while we were at a competition.

00:00:17.737 --> 00:00:19.977
One of the girls had said,
“Oh, they're from Compton,

00:00:19.977 --> 00:00:24.144
they probably have bullet holes
in their barn or something.”

00:00:25.126 --> 00:00:29.293
To ride for Compton, there
comes a sense of pride for it.

00:00:32.573 --> 00:00:35.156
(gentle music)

00:00:41.977 --> 00:00:44.803
My name is Shola Oyefeso, I'm 17 years old

00:00:44.803 --> 00:00:47.279
and I'm a student at The
Compton Junior Posse.

00:00:47.279 --> 00:00:49.319
- [Instructor] Looks great,
bend your knee though.

00:00:49.319 --> 00:00:53.486
- A program that keeps kids
on horses and off the streets.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.020
- I've been riding with
The Compton Junior Posse

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:01.020
for about six years now.

00:01:02.078 --> 00:01:06.128
I am one of the more experienced
riders in the program.

00:01:06.128 --> 00:01:09.571
I have learned a lot about myself.

00:01:09.571 --> 00:01:12.640
I definitely have more patience
after working with horses.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:14.860
Like, when I first started
riding at like 11 years old,

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:19.004
I used to always get in
trouble from attitude problems.

00:01:19.004 --> 00:01:21.074
You come in with a bad
attitude when you're trying

00:01:21.074 --> 00:01:24.607
to ride a horse and it
comes out through them, too.

00:01:24.607 --> 00:01:26.774
It's like you're in sync with your horse,

00:01:26.774 --> 00:01:30.941
you're supposed to be in
sync, it's a partnership.

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:35.000
(upbeat music)

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.743
We do have serious competitors at The
Compton Jr. Posse. 

00:01:37.743 --> 00:01:41.298
We go to a show per month just 
to show what kind of progress that we’ve been doing

00:01:41.298 --> 00:01:45.091
and what kind of work we’re doing with the kids.  

00:01:45.091 --> 00:01:50.607
We’re coming out there and 
competing with the upper level people.

00:01:50.607 --> 00:01:58.022
I came in fourth for the medal finals at the 
Interscholastic Equestrian League Competition — that’s a big deal. 

00:01:58.022 --> 00:02:05.381
It is a stereotype that more people
in the horse world are white and rich, 

00:02:05.381 --> 00:02:09.548
but there are more people from different backgrounds
and different demographics

00:02:09.548 --> 00:02:16.000
that are competing now; it feels 
good to break the stereotype.

